@description "Scope: innermost policy wins, atom-local wins over all"

# @scope attaches modifiers to every atom within its braces. Nested
# scopes override on a per-modifier-name basis: the inner value wins,
# unrelated modifiers from outer scopes survive. Atom-local modifiers
# beat every scope level.
#
# The 1ms outer timeout would kill the 20ms sleep if stacking were
# additive. Success proves replacement, not accumulation. The payload
# is a map so that sleep's own @{ duration_ms: 20 } argument merges
# cleanly without wrapping the value in a __root__ sentinel.

@scope :timeout=1ms {
  @scope :timeout=1s {
    const @{ value: { tag: "ok" } } -> sleep @{ duration_ms: 20 }
  }
}

@assert: result.tag == "ok"
